.el .ds Aq '
.TH bhtune-restore-loop 1  "bhtune-restore-loop "
.SH NAME
bhtune\-restore\-loop \- Restore the recorded pre\-tune loop values after an explicitly recoverable orphan
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbhtune\-restore\-loop\fR [\fB\-\-bridge\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIRUN_ID\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Restore the recorded pre\-tune loop values after an explicitly recoverable orphan
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bridge\-host\fR \fI<BRIDGE_HOST>\fR
Cross\-check the run\*(Aqs recorded OPC bridge host; never selects a different gateway
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Cross\-check the run\*(Aqs recorded OPC server; never selects a different controller
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Confirm the live restore. Required; no interactive prompt is offered
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR [default: table]
How to print the per\-step restore report
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
table: Human\-readable text (default)
.IP \(bu 2
json: Pretty\-printed JSON. This is the external contract for scripted/scheduled consumers, so its shape must not change silently once shipped
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIRUN_ID\fR>
ID of the failed run marked explicitly eligible by the Full\-mode orphan sweep
